<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Mohács</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1526</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-hungarian-wars">Ottoman–Hungarian wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Mohács was fought in 1526 in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suleiman-the-magnificent">Suleiman the Magnificent</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-hungary">Kingdom of Hungary</a>. The Hungarian army was annihilated and King Louis II died during the retreat. The victory led to the partition of Hungary and opened the way to the first Ottoman siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> in 1529.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-mohacs.jpg" alt="Battle of Mohács" width="320" height="244" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: unknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_moh%C3%A1csi_csata_(Des_T%C3%BCrckischen_Keysers_Solymon_schlacht_-_So_mit_dem_K%C3%BCnig_von_Hungern_gethan,_Bamberg,_1526).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
